| image       = Jade.png
| description = This gem pulses with energy, almost as if it were a living thing.
| id          = GemstoneGreen
| type        = Material
| source      = [[Charred Fortress]]
| usage       = Crafting, Upgrading
| weight      = 2.0
| stack       = 50
| teleport    = Yes
}}

'''Jade''' is a material used to craft the "Nature" version of some [[Ashlands]] weapons. They have a chance to be found in the [[Charred chest]]s inside [[Charred Fortress|Charred Fortresses]] located in Ashlands.

A weapon upgraded with Jade gains 10 [[Poison]] damage, and their hit effect has a 20% chance to [[Immobilized|immobilize]] the target for 10 seconds.

== Usage ==
=== Crafting ===
* {{Item link|Klossen}}
* {{Item link|Nidhögg the Primal}}
* {{Item link|Primal Berserkir Axes}}
* {{Item link|Primal Slayer}}
* {{Item link|Root Fang}}
* {{Item link|Root Ripper}}
* {{Item link|Splitnir the Primal}}
* {{Item link|Staff of the Wild}}

== Trivia ==
*There is a creature (internal ID "Goblin_Gem") that never appears in the actual game, but can be spawned using the console, that drops all three kinds of Ashlands gemstones.
*In real-life, jade — particularly Type A (natural, untreated jadeite form of the mineral) — is revered for its symbolism of purity, harmony, and protection in various cultures, qualities that are inherently linked to the earth element. This could be attribute to Nature properties this material endowed to some Ashland weapons.

== See also ==
*{{Item link|Bloodstone}}
*{{Item link|Iolite}}

